The first statement ignores lines shorter than 3 characters, causing valid short lines to be treated as continuations of the previous line. This leads to incorrect parsing behavior. The second statement checks if the last character of a line is a continuation character ('\'), which can further exacerbate the issue by allowing short lines to improperly extend the previous line.

